|p34;DIMENSIONS TO INCLUDE:\P}-^Ipole to property line\P-^Ipole to closest building\P-^Istreet width\P-^IROW width\P{\fTahoma|b1|i0|c0|p34;-^IDO NOT ADD ADDITIONAL DIMENSIONS} \P{\fTahoma|b1|i0|c0|p34;FOLLOW CURRENT DIMENSION FORMATTING}\P{\fTahoma|b1|i0|
  3
c0|p34;\P\fTahoma|b0|i0|c0|p34;\LEXISTING:}\P-^Iexisting utilities (show once for each and use "typ.")\P-^Iexisting manholes & handholes\P-^Ipower source for pole (IF KNOWN)\P-^Istreet names (the street the pole is located on will be a "field" and alread
  3
y filled in for you)\P-^Iexisting street lights\P- existing structures (i.e. sidewalk). Use these notes sparingly and not in the way of other information\P\P{\LPROPOSED:}\P-^Iproposed pole (this note also contains existing info)\P- (2) proposed handhol
  3
e\P\P------\P{\L\P}- ONLY SHOW UTILITIES AND/OR MANHOLES OF ANY KIND IN THIS VIEW, AND ONLY IF THEY ARE WITHIN 50 FEET OF POLE. ERASE ALL OTHERS\P\P- CENTER STREET NAME BETWEEN ARROWS\P\P- ONLY SHOW STREET NAME / ARROWS COMBO ONCE PER STREET\P\P- FEN
  3
CELINE LINETYPE SHOULD ALWAYS HAVE A LINETYPE SCALE OF 0.25\P\P- NEW DIMENSION: ADD DIM FOR DISTANCE FROM POLE TO CURB. MAKE SURE THIS DIM MATCHES DETAIL 2 ON PAGE 6. \P\P- (2) NEW HANDHOLE TYPICALLY GOES IN LANDSCAPING WHEN POSSIBLE, NOT SIDEWALK \P
  1
\P- NO TEMP LIGHTING BASE \P\P- NO TREE INFO / FENCING\P\P- NO AZIMUTH INFO\P\P-PLEASE SHOW %%P AFTER EVERY DIMENSION\P\P- USE "X'-X" %%P CURB TO CURB" FOR STREET DIMENSION FORMATTING
